  "card": "This PR moves the assignment of HTTPRemoteClient::m_keep_alive inside m_send_mutex and changes it from an atomic boolean to a mutex-guarded boolean. Previously, when a client pipelined a keep-alive request followed by a Connection: close request, a worker thread handling the second request cleared the keep-alive flag before acquiring the buffer lock. If the I/O thread finished sending the first reply in between, it saw an empty buffer and a cleared keep-alive flag, disconnecting the client and dropping the pending second response. The PR adds a unit test using a mock socket that deterministically triggers this race condition and fails without the fix.",
